/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - An n-to-2ⁿ decoder has n input bits and 2ⁿ output lines.
   - Inside is an AND plane.
   - Yi = 1 ⇔ (bn−1 … b0) = i
   - Here Yi is output line i; bn−1…b0 is the input code; i is the line number from 0 to 2ⁿ−1.
   - An enable input turns the whole decoder on or off.
   - A 2:1 multiplexer has data inputs D0 and D1, select S, and output Y.
   - A mux tree builds wider multiplexers.
   - Shannon expansion makes the mux a logic element.
   - A 1-bit equality gate is an XNOR: E = A·B + A′·B′.
   - The magnitude cell compares one bit pair and carries the decision.
*/
