/* book exam traps: Treating active-low decoder outputs as active-high: an active-low selected line is 0, so ORing selected lines does not give the sum of minterms; use NAND or invert. | Building a large decoder from smaller ones without using the enable as the extra address bit; the MSB must enable the correct half. | Letting a comparator decide from the LSB end. The first differing MSB decides, and later bits cannot override it. | Forgetting that a tristate bus needs exactly one enabled driver: two drivers cause contention, none causes a floating bus. | Confusing a multiplexer's select lines with its data inputs in Shannon expansion, or tying a data input to a variable that is also a select. */
